            "**Against health education:** health education informs and teaches, assuming that knowledge produces action; social marketing researches the consumer first, segments the audience, engineers an attractive exchange, manipulates price and place as well as promotion, and monitors continuously so the offer can be adapted. Social marketing = health education + the marketing mix + consumer orientation.",
