            "**Price:** the monetary price, deliberately subsidised but usually **not zero**, because a nominal price signals value, reduces wastage and gives the retailer a margin to stock and push it; and the **non-monetary price** - time, travel, waiting, pain, embarrassment, lost wages, lost pleasure and social disapproval - which is often the larger barrier and the more rewarding one to attack.",
